t Colorado -- by simply tuning out the noise.","published":"2026-11-24T21:29:37.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585728/colorado-sanders-shrugs-hot-seat-chatter-ucf","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Memphis' Charles Huff says he's not candidate for Maryland head coaching job","description":"Memphis' Charles Huff said he's not a candidate for the head coaching vacancy at Maryland and will not be part of this year's coaching carousel.","published":"2026-11-24T20:33:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585465/charles-huff-says-not-candidate-maryland-hc-job","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NCAA sanctions Liberty over tampering with two players before entering portal","description":"Among the penalties the NCAA announced against Liberty, two coaches and the GM received show-cause penalties over tampering.","published":"2026-11-24T20:05:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585093/ncaa-sanctions-liberty-transfer-portal-tampering","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Five-star OT Lincoln Fa'alafi commits to Notre Dame, to join 2028 class","description":"New Zealand native Lincoln Fa'alafi, ESPN's No. 8 overall prospect in the 2028 cycle, committed Tuesday to Notre Dame.","published":"2026-11-24T19:56:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584881/notre-dame-gets-2028-commitment-ot-lincoln-faalafi","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"A timeline of Michigan athletics since 2017","description":"Warde Manuel's eventful decade in Ann Arbor has been marked by athletic successes and marred by controversy.","published":"2026-11-24T18:47:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49351177/2026-michigan-warde-manuel-athletic-department-tenure-line-investigation","type":"Story","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios in Week 13?","description":"Plenty of spots are still up for grabs entering the final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-24T18:22:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50583399/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-13","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Trev Alberts told he won't be Michigan AD after agreement","description":"Trev Alberts was \"shocked and disheartened\" to be informed by the search firm representing Michigan that he will not be the Wolverines' next AD, he told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-24T23:50:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50583155/attorney-trev-alberts-told-next-ad-michigan","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Dan Wetzel","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4702828/aj-holmes-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A._J._Holmes_Jr."},"pick":{"pick":42,"round":2,"team":"TB","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"A. J. Holmes Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A._J._Holmes_Jr.","description":"American football player (born 2003)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:12Z","intro":"Anthony \"A. J.\" Holmes Jr. (born November 7, 2003) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Texas Tech Red Raiders. He previously played for the Houston Cougars.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Holmes Jr. attended Westfield High School in Houston, Texas. As a senior season, he was named the District 14-6A MVP. Coming out of high school, Holmes Jr. committed to play college football for the Houston Cougars over other offers from schools such as TCU, Kansas State, Washington State, SMU, and Virginia."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"HOUSTON\nDuring his freshman season in 2022, Holmes Jr. notched six tackles with half a tackle being for a loss. In the 2023 season, he appeared in 12 games with three starts, where he totaled 21 tackles with four and a half going for a loss, and two and a half sacks. During the 2024 season, Holmes Jr. tallied 40 tackles with eight and a half being for a loss, and two sacks. After the season, he entered his name into the NCAA transfer portal.\n\nTEXAS TECH\nHolmes Jr. transferred to play for the Texas Tech Red Raiders. In week 2 of the 2025 season, he notched four tackles with two being for a loss, a sack, a pass deflection, and a fumble recovery in a blowout win over Kent State. In week 6, Holmes Jr. recorded two sacks in a win versus Kansas. In week 7, he recorded a sack against Arizona State. For his performance during the 2025 season, Holmes Jr. was named a first-team All-American by Pro Football Focus."}]}}